.TH PING 1 "2026-05-22" "hako" "hako utilities"
.SH NAME
ping \- send ICMP echo requests and report round-trip times
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ping
.RI [@ nameserver ]
.I host
.RB [ \-c
.IR count ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ping
sends ICMP echo-request packets to
.I host
and prints the round-trip time (RTT) for each reply.
.I host
may be an IPv4 address or a hostname; if a hostname is given it is resolved
to an IPv4 address via DNS before the first packet is sent.
.PP
A one-second pause is inserted between successive probes.
After all probes, a statistics summary is printed showing the number of packets
transmitted and received, the packet-loss percentage, and the minimum, average,
and maximum RTTs.
.PP
By default the nameserver
.B 8.8.8.8
is used for hostname resolution.
An alternate resolver can be given with
.BI @ address
before the host argument.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-c " count
Send
.I count
probes.
Defaults to
.BR 4 .
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B "ping 8.8.8.8"
Ping Google's public DNS server four times.
.TP
.B "ping -c 10 example.com"
Send ten probes to
.BR example.com .
.TP
.B "ping @1.1.1.1 -c 1 example.com"
Use Cloudflare's resolver and send one probe.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All probes completed (some may have timed out).
.TP
.B 1
Missing or invalid arguments, or hostname resolution failed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ping (8),
.BR hako (1)
